Z||000006||JBGehling||08-09-2001||11:10 PM||||BTW, the times posted in that Official Sales Brochure are nearly a second off. Pontiac probably just stated such poor times for insurance purposes. <P>As slow as 16 in the 1/4 mile sounds today... back in 85, that was a dang quick car. You could race a brand-new IROC-Z and not lose too badly (maybe about a car-length). And that's a big ol' 350 vs. an engine more than half it's size! (of course, I'm talking 85 vs. 85... 88 IROC vs. 88 GT is a much different story.<P>Josh<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||banditbalz||08-24-2001||11:19 PM||||formula2, you may want to read the fine print. That's a '88 brochure and specs were measured at a lower RPM level. I am correct at 140 hp and 173lb/ft. torque. By the way, my stock 86 GT has run a 15.2 at 90 mph. Only aftermarket part is a K+N air filter. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/banditbalz_17.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||14
Z||000008||Dave Gunsul||08-25-2001||02:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JBGehling:<P>As slow as 16 in the 1/4 mile sounds today... back in 85, that was a dang quick car. You could race a brand-new IROC-Z and not lose too badly (maybe about a car-length). And that's a big ol' 350 vs. an engine more than half it's size! (of course, I'm talking 85 vs. 85... 88 IROC vs. 88 GT is a much different story.<P>Josh<P>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Only bad thing about that theory is that you couldn't get a 350 in an Iroc until 87!<P>BTW 85 GT= 140 HP.  170 IB. FT.<BR>weight: 2572.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
